E13 shows all 5 failing orders come from supplier "Red Sea Parts" with orders created at t=506-508, and the invoice_text format appears truncated/different ("Amount: 298..." without VAT/total fields visible). E14 shows ledger syncs are normal and pre-date the anomaly — sync-job is not writing bad data into orders.

The sync-job hypothesis is now refuted: ledger rows look healthy and sync-job writes to `ledger`, not `orders`. The failing invoices all share the same supplier and started arriving around t=505-508, pointing to a supplier-side format change.

I'll use my last investigation to confirm the invoice layout difference vs baseline orders from the same supplier.

